-- title:
--   Places above P determined by their centre on 𝒪_P[κ']
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be a field, $F$ a field extension of $\kappa$, and $\kappa'$ a field extension of $\kappa$ that is algebraic and separable over $\kappa$. Let $F'$ be a field carrying compatible algebra structures over $\kappa'$, over $F$ and over $\kappa$, with $\kappa \to F \to F'$ and $\kappa \to \kappa' \to F'$ scalar towers, such that $F'$ is integral over $F$, and assume $F'$ is generated as an $F$-algebra by the image of $\kappa'$, i.e. $\mathrm{Algebra.adjoin}\,F(\mathrm{range}(\kappa' \to F')) = \top$. Let $P$ be a place of $F$ over $\kappa$, that is, a valuation subring $\mathcal{O}_P \subseteq F$ containing the image of $\kappa$, different from $F$ itself, and a principal ideal ring; and let $W_1, W_2$ be two such places of $F'$ over $\kappa'$, with valuation subrings $\mathcal{O}_{W_1}, \mathcal{O}_{W_2}$. Suppose both lie above $P$, in the sense that the preimage of $\mathcal{O}_{W_i}$ under $F \to F'$ equals $\mathcal{O}_P$ for $i = 1,2$. Suppose further that for every $x$ in the subring of $F'$ generated by the image of $\mathcal{O}_P$ together with the image of $\kappa'$, one has $x \in \mathrm{nonunits}(\mathcal{O}_{W_1})$, i.e. $W_1$-valuation less than one, if and only if $x \in \mathrm{nonunits}(\mathcal{O}_{W_2})$. Then $W_1 = W_2$ as places.
--
--   This is the uniqueness half of the classical theory of extensions of a place along a separable constant field extension: a place of $F' = F\cdot\kappa'$ above $P$ is pinned down by its centre on the subring $\mathcal{O}_P[\kappa']$, whose localisations at its maximal ideals exhaust such places. It is used in the rigid-analytic node-annulus constructions, where places of a constant-field extension must be recognised from their behaviour on this generated subring, and in the compatibility of this recognition with automorphisms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Place_eq_of_comap_eq_of_forall_mem_nonunits_iff.lean

